Credits
=======

ktpls builds on the work of these projects and resources:

* gopls, the Go language server
  https://github.com/golang/tools/tree/master/gopls
  Copyright 2009 The Go Authors. BSD 3-Clause License.
  The architecture of ktpls is modeled on gopls: the split into command,
  protocol, server, cache and language packages, one server file per LSP
  feature, editor-buffer overlays, and byte-offset/UTF-16 position mapping.
  No gopls source code is included.

* tree-sitter-kotlin, the Kotlin grammar for tree-sitter
  https://github.com/fwcd/tree-sitter-kotlin
  Copyright (c) 2019 fwcd. MIT License.
  Its generated parser and external scanner are compiled into ktpls.

* tree-sitter, the incremental parsing library
  https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter
  Copyright (c) 2018 Max Brunsfeld. MIT License.
  The parsing runtime, compiled into ktpls through go-tree-sitter.

* go-tree-sitter, the Go bindings for tree-sitter
  https://github.com/tree-sitter/go-tree-sitter
  Copyright (c) 2024 Amaan Qureshi. MIT License.

* go-pointer, a dependency of go-tree-sitter
  https://github.com/mattn/go-pointer
  Copyright (c) 2019 Yasuhiro Matsumoto. MIT License.

* Kotlin LSP by JetBrains
  https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlin-lsp
  The reference for which capabilities a Kotlin language server should
  offer. No code from it is included.

* The Language Server Protocol specification, by Microsoft
  https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/
  The protocol types of ktpls are written from the specification.

* mason.nvim
  https://github.com/mason-org/mason.nvim
  editors/nvim provides a registry in Mason's package format. No code from
  it is included.

The full license texts of the third-party code compiled into ktpls are in
